acant everybody's short workers and the  big solution for us is to get this  foreign workers program uh in place and  and acting as it should  the bc restaurant association wants the  province to ask ottawa for an exemption  to what's called the labor market impact  assessment which confirms there is a  need for a temporary foreign worker for  any given job and that there is no  canadian or permanent resident available  to do that job  this would be temporary and could help  fill the void by speeding up the process  we're pushing the feds not only to  reduce the time but we're also pushing  them to give us more levers and more say  in what type of workers we need because  we know what we need working all these  eyes sometimes drains you it's very  exhausting also i was working seven days  a week  um now i'm down to five days a week um  but i mean that's what you got to do  when times are tough you got to help  each other out and fill in spots when  needed you all ready for a big weekend  kate  in the meantime those already picking up  the slack we'll continue to ask for  patience especially during the busy  weekends ahead emadikahi global news  women run the world cup ahead the first  female referees of soccer's biggest  tournament  [Music]  just six months until canada's men's  national team will make its first  appearance at a fifa world cup in 36  years and this tournament will also be  making history by having female referees  take charge of men's world cup games for  the very first time redmond shannon  reports  referees warming up together just before  the last men's world cup a boys only  club for almost a century that is until  now  fifa says for the first time three of  the 36 referees at soccer's biggest  tournament will be women with three more  female assistant referees along the  sidelines in qatar canadian carol ann  chenard worked at nine different fifa  tournaments including olympic games and  junior mail events as female referees  we've always just wanted to be  considered a referee  but the opportunities over the last four  years have just grown leaps and bounds  across the the world in many ways this  announcement is the end game thanks to  pioneers like chanard women like her  have been refereeing men at lower levels  for years but the world cup will mark a  new milestone with the whole world  watching the head of fifa's referees  committee said i would hope that in the  future the selection of elite women's  match officials for important men's  competitions will be perceived as  something normal and no longer as  sensational the journey to get here has  been about building experience but also  respect something that hasn't always  been shown to women in charge in 2020  argentinian star sergio aguero was  criticized for putting his arm around a  female official when he didn't agree  with her call of course there are  comments oh it's a girl oh it's a female  that kind of thing and yes there have  been statements and comments made to me  during a game but i manage that just  like i would any other type of statement  it is remarkable that this progress is  being made at a world cup in qatar in a  region where some countries lag behind  engender equality teams from iran and  saudi arabia could play their world cup  games with female officials countries  that until recent years banned women  from even watching men play never mind  taking charge redmond shannon global  news london  finding your true fit  next the group helping people thread  together their gender journeys  [Music]  the clothes you wear can sometimes be a  reflection of your personality  preferences and identity a student-led  initiative is teaching members of  calgary's lgbtq community how to alter  clothing to make them gender-affirming  as jill croteau reports some consider it  a lifeline  there's a saying that goes you can have  anything you want in life if you dress  for it  what if that want is to simply be  accepted as your true authentic self a  desire to look how you feel on the  inside  that's why every stitch is so  significant so i identify as a trans man  non-binary in that sense but yeah i  transitioned from female to male when i  was 15. this workshop is organized by  threads that thrive  it's run by state students for students  and it's where people learn how to alter  clothes to fit their bodies garments  tailored to be gender affirming it  lights you up having something that i  want to wear and represent myself in  makes me feel like i want to get out of  my house and i think that's helpful for  a lot of lgbt people who do suffer with  agoraphobia depression anxiety and other  things that are so relevant to our  community shopping in designated men or  women's departments can be intimidating  and sometimes risky for those who are  navigating their own gender journeys  when you are  a queer person shopping in  a clothing store that maybe doesn't  match your outward gender expression um  fear of being outed fear of being  persecuted it can be dangerous  people are not always fitting in these  neat little buckets so it started years  ago when they started acknowledging that  hey not everyone is a size zero to  whatever there are people that fall  outside of that so they started to make  things maybe a bit more size inclusive  and now i think they are making strides  towards making things more gender  inclusive while they're learning the  skills they need to make clothes that  fit  turns out it's truly about the space  that fits it's life-saving definitely  there's something in me that's still  afraid that my right to be trans will  get taken away like they're going to  take away my hormones they're going to  reverse my surgery and give me girl  clothes again and the fact that i know  that i have the support there it's not  so much the clothing so much as the  the pathways that are opening up for me  to get it joe crotell global news  and that is global national for this  sunday night i'm tracy tong  tonight's canada is the sunrise in  sylvan lake alberta we love seeing your  canada so please keep sending your  photos to viewers at globalnational.com  thanks for watching colleen christie  will be at the anchor desk tomorrow have  a great night
 

